  "decision_conditions": [
    "Occupier",
    "The development must be begun not later than the expiration of three years beginning with the date hereof.\r\rReason: To comply with Section 91 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990, as amended.",
    "All external facing materials, treatments and finishes shall be similar to those of the original building and maintained and retained thereafter. This applies unless differences are shown on the drawings we have approved. \r\rReason: To ensure that the extension harmonises with the existing building and to ensure compliance with Policy 28 of the Sutton Local Plan 2018.",
    "Prior to the commencement of development, further details of the proposed solar PV system must be submitted to the Local Planning Authority and approved in writing, including:\r(i) a plan showing the number and orientation of the solar PV panels proposed for  each unit and the total area of the proposed array; \r(ii) product specifications including the power output of each panel and maintenance  requirements; and\r(iii) confirmation of the annual amount of electricity expected to be generated and  associated CO2 savings.\r\rReason: To comply with Policy 31 of the Sutton Local Plan 2018.",
    "The development hereby approved shall be constructed in accordance with the approved Energy Statement (version 1.0) prepared by Energi IQ Ltd and dated 4 November 2025 together with the approved solar PV details. Prior to first occupation of the dwellings, 'as-built' Standard Assessment Procedure (SAP) outputs must be submitted to the Local Planning Authority and approved in writing to demonstrate that the proposed development has achieved the targeted reduction in carbon dioxide (CO2) emissions. All of the approved measures must thereafter be retained for as long \ras the development is in existence. \r\rReason: To comply with Policy 31 of the Sutton Local Plan 2018.",
    "The development must be carried out in accordance with the provisions of the Fire Strategy.\r\rReason: To ensure that the development incorporates the necessary fire safety measures in accordance with the Mayor's London Plan Policy D12."
  ],
